WEBVTT

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:39.615
You're entering the vicinity
of an area adjacent to a location.

00:00:39.698 --> 00:00:41.867
The kind of place where
there might be a monster

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.619
or some kind of weird mirror.

00:00:43.702 --> 00:00:44.912
These are just examples.

00:00:44.995 --> 00:00:47.039
It could also
be something much better.

00:00:47.122 --> 00:00:48.540
Prepare to enter...

00:00:58.383 --> 00:01:03.180
As per your request, please find enclosed
the last man on earth.

00:01:04.556 --> 00:01:06.517
Finally... Solitude.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.270
I can read books
for all eternity.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.773
It's not fair.

00:01:12.856 --> 00:01:14.608
It's not fair!

00:01:14.691 --> 00:01:17.110
Wait. My eyes aren't that bad.

00:01:17.194 --> 00:01:20.614
I can still read
the large-print books.

00:01:22.199 --> 00:01:23.367
It's not f...

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.120
Well, lucky I know
how to read braille.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.375
Hey, look at that weird mirror.

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:34.336
Cursed by his own hubris.

00:01:34.419 --> 00:01:37.214
There's a political debate on.
Quick, change the channel.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:40.676
Hey, that's what Fry said
when we turned onthe debate.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:44.346
C-SPAN9 presents
The Thrill of Politics.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.060
Wha...

00:01:50.144 --> 00:01:52.104
Look, I know there
are no car chases,

00:01:52.187 --> 00:01:53.564
but this is important.

00:01:53.647 --> 00:01:56.275
One of these two men will
become president of the world.

00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:58.710
What do we care?
We live in the United States.

00:01:58.794 --> 00:02:01.088
The United States
is part of the world.

00:02:01.171 --> 00:02:03.340
Wow, I have been
gone a long time.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.342
It's time someone
had the courage

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.201
to stand up and say

00:02:07.298 --> 00:02:09.763
I'm against those things
that everybody hates!

00:02:09.846 --> 00:02:11.807
Now, I respect my opponent.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.433
I think he's a good man.

00:02:13.517 --> 00:02:17.604
But, quite frankly, I agree
with everything he just said!

00:02:17.688 --> 00:02:21.191
These are the candidates?
They sound like clones.

00:02:21.275 --> 00:02:23.527
Wait a minute.
They are clones!

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.862
Don't let their
identical DNA fool you.

00:02:25.946 --> 00:02:27.698
They differ on
some key issues.

00:02:27.781 --> 00:02:31.285
I say your 3 cent
titanium tax goes too far.

00:02:31.368 --> 00:02:34.162
And I say your
3 cent titanium tax

00:02:34.246 --> 00:02:36.081
doesn't go
too far enough.

00:02:36.164 --> 00:02:39.042
If I were registered to vote,
I'd send these clowns a message

00:02:39.126 --> 00:02:42.129
by staying home on election day
and dressing up like a clown!

00:02:42.212 --> 00:02:43.338
You're not registered?

00:02:43.422 --> 00:02:45.090
Nope. Not vaccinated, either.

00:02:45.173 --> 00:02:48.343
Besides, it's not like one vote
ever made a difference.

00:02:48.427 --> 00:02:49.636
That's not true.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.389
The first robot president
won by exactly one vote.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.641
Ah, yes! John Quincy Adding Machine.

00:02:54.725 --> 00:02:56.685
He struck a chord
with the voters

00:02:56.768 --> 00:02:59.521
when he pledged not to
go on a killing spree.

00:02:59.605 --> 00:03:01.106
But, like most politicians,

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:03.692
he promised more
than he could deliver.

00:03:03.775 --> 00:03:06.236
The point is,
one vote can make a difference.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.571
And even though it won't,

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.698
I'm still taking you
to get registered.

00:03:09.781 --> 00:03:12.159
Yes, that's a capital idea.

00:03:12.242 --> 00:03:14.202
Let's all go register.

00:03:14.286 --> 00:03:16.914
Professor, when did you become
so obsessed with voting?

00:03:16.997 --> 00:03:19.499
The very instant I became old.

00:03:27.758 --> 00:03:29.092
The problem with both parties

00:03:29.176 --> 00:03:31.386
is that they always
want to give your tax dollars

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.763
to the less fortunate.

00:03:32.846 --> 00:03:34.848
The less fortunate get all the breaks.

00:03:34.932 --> 00:03:38.185
You know, Fry, you could
join a third party, maybe.

00:03:38.268 --> 00:03:40.896
Only weirdos and mutants
join third parties.

00:03:41.021 --> 00:03:44.650
Really? I better keep an eye out
at the next meeting.

00:03:44.733 --> 00:03:46.401
What party do you belong to, Bender?

00:03:46.485 --> 00:03:47.986
I'm not allowed to vote.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.112
'Cause you're a robot?

00:03:49.196 --> 00:03:50.864
No. Convicted felon.

00:03:58.038 --> 00:03:59.748
We favor unreasonably
huge subsidies

00:03:59.831 --> 00:04:02.251
to the Brain Slug planet.

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:04.670
Okay, but what are
the brain slugs who control you

00:04:04.753 --> 00:04:06.296
going to do
for the working man?

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.131
Attach brain slugs to them.

00:04:08.215 --> 00:04:10.175
Sure, you say that now.

00:04:12.219 --> 00:04:13.512
So is it true you can make

00:04:13.595 --> 00:04:15.847
all kinds of shirts
and ropes out of hemp?

00:04:15.931 --> 00:04:17.766
Dave's not here, man.

00:04:17.849 --> 00:04:20.310
I also heard hemp
makes great shampoo.

00:04:20.394 --> 00:04:21.937
It does? No way!

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.481
I got to check out this brochure.

00:04:28.235 --> 00:04:30.279
So, what are you doing
to protect

00:04:30.362 --> 00:04:33.448
my constitutional right
to bear doomsday devices?

00:04:33.532 --> 00:04:35.617
Well, first off,
we're going to get rid

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:38.829
of that 3-day waiting
period for mad scientists.

00:04:38.912 --> 00:04:40.330
Damn straight!

00:04:40.414 --> 00:04:43.333
Today, the mad scientist
can't get a doomsday device.

00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:45.502
Tomorrow, it's the mad grad student!

00:04:45.586 --> 00:04:47.045
Where will it end?

00:04:47.129 --> 00:04:48.547
Amen, brother!

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.133
I don't go anywhere
without my mutated anthrax...

00:04:51.216 --> 00:04:52.801
for duck huntin'.

00:04:52.885 --> 00:04:55.178
Sure, humans are cute

00:04:55.262 --> 00:04:57.264
but how else are we supposed
to test cosmetics?

00:04:57.347 --> 00:04:59.266
I concur.

00:05:00.475 --> 00:05:03.854
Now here's a party I can
get excited about. Sign me up.

00:05:03.937 --> 00:05:06.023
Sorry, not with that attitude.

00:05:06.106 --> 00:05:07.482
Okay, then screw it.

00:05:07.566 --> 00:05:09.192
Welcome aboard, brother!

00:05:09.276 --> 00:05:11.111
- All right!
- You're out.

00:05:14.156 --> 00:05:15.198
That was pretty cool.

00:05:15.282 --> 00:05:17.993
I think I'm actually starting
to get interested in politics.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:27.502
And so, with two weeks
left in the campaign,

00:05:27.586 --> 00:05:29.171
the question on everyone's mind

00:05:29.254 --> 00:05:31.840
is who will be
the next president of earth.

00:05:31.924 --> 00:05:36.094
Jack Johnson,
or bitter rival John Jackson?

00:05:36.178 --> 00:05:38.388
Two terrific candidates, huh, Morbo?

00:05:38.472 --> 00:05:42.059
All humans are vermin
in the eyes of Morbo.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.146
In other local news,

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:49.233
disaster struck on
Saturn's moon of Titan today

00:05:49.316 --> 00:05:51.193
when a titanium mine collapsed

00:05:51.276 --> 00:05:53.153
trapping 1,000 robot workers.

00:05:53.237 --> 00:05:55.489
What? Lord have mercy!

00:05:55.572 --> 00:05:57.199
Unless something is done quickly,

00:05:57.282 --> 00:06:00.285
the trapped robots
will be dead within 300 years.

00:06:00.369 --> 00:06:03.372
Sir, what rescue operations
are planned?

00:06:03.455 --> 00:06:06.375
The plan is, basically,
to pave over the area

00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:08.168
and get on with our lives.

00:06:09.336 --> 00:06:10.879
News of the mine's closing

00:06:10.963 --> 00:06:12.965
sent titanium prices skyrocketing.

00:06:13.048 --> 00:06:14.091
All right! I'm rich!

00:06:14.174 --> 00:06:15.342
What are you talking about?

00:06:15.425 --> 00:06:17.261
My body's 40% titanium.

00:06:17.344 --> 00:06:21.431
I'm finally richer than
those snooty ATM machines.

00:06:21.515 --> 00:06:22.933
Too bad you can't spend it.

00:06:23.016 --> 00:06:25.686
- Oh, can't I?
- No.

00:06:25.769 --> 00:06:27.646
Watch me, poor man.

00:06:29.147 --> 00:06:30.566
Pleasure doin' business with you.

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:34.570
Game's over, losers!

00:06:34.653 --> 00:06:36.446
I have all the money.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:39.992
Compare your lives to mine
and then kill yourselves.

00:06:41.243 --> 00:06:43.161
Hey, get away! Shoo!

00:06:43.328 --> 00:06:46.790
I'll give you $5 to not do
what you're thinking about doing.

00:06:50.252 --> 00:06:52.546
You just lost $5.

00:06:57.759 --> 00:06:59.261
Hey, buddy! Little help?

00:07:00.262 --> 00:07:01.805
Thank you!

00:07:05.142 --> 00:07:06.852
Hello, peasants.

00:07:06.935 --> 00:07:08.854
Bender! What happened to you?

00:07:08.937 --> 00:07:10.939
You look different.
Did you get a haircut?

00:07:11.023 --> 00:07:13.233
No! I sold my body.

00:07:13.942 --> 00:07:15.861
Sold your body?

00:07:15.986 --> 00:07:18.155
Oh, Bender, I've been down that road.

00:07:18.238 --> 00:07:21.241
I know it's glamorous
and the parties are great,

00:07:21.325 --> 00:07:23.285
but you'll end up spending
every dollar you make

00:07:23.368 --> 00:07:25.454
on jewelry and skintight pants.

00:07:25.621 --> 00:07:26.705
This is crazy, Bender.

00:07:26.788 --> 00:07:28.624
How are you going to live
without a body?

00:07:28.916 --> 00:07:31.793
Bodies are for hookers and fat people.

00:07:31.877 --> 00:07:35.130
All I need is a wad of cash
with a head wrapped around it.

00:07:35.213 --> 00:07:37.466
Well, at least now
you can pay off your loan shark.

00:07:37.549 --> 00:07:40.344
Yeah, right, what's he going to do,
break my legs?

00:07:42.554 --> 00:07:44.640
Ah! This is the life!

00:07:44.723 --> 00:07:47.100
Another martini, please!

00:07:49.561 --> 00:07:52.564
Shaken, not stirred.

00:07:52.648 --> 00:07:54.983
Oh, yeah!

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:00.155
Put it all on black.

00:08:00.239 --> 00:08:02.032
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa!

00:08:07.246 --> 00:08:09.122
Twenty-one red.

00:08:10.332 --> 00:08:12.292
I beg your pardon.
33 black.

00:08:12.376 --> 00:08:13.752
Yes!

00:08:13.835 --> 00:08:15.212
The rich get richer.

00:08:26.473 --> 00:08:29.017
Strike! In your face, Leela!

00:08:47.369 --> 00:08:48.662
Timber!

00:08:50.831 --> 00:08:53.166
Hey, Bender, can I take
a ride in your car?

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:54.876
Maybe if you clean up first.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.004
It looks like your neck
stepped in something.

00:08:57.588 --> 00:08:58.880
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:08:58.964 --> 00:09:00.882
That's just your body.

00:09:03.135 --> 00:09:05.804
Hey, you look me
in the shins and say that.

00:09:05.888 --> 00:09:08.473
Hey, I've had it
up to here with this place.

00:09:08.557 --> 00:09:10.017
I'm off
to the head museum

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.269
to hang out
with classy heads like me

00:09:12.352 --> 00:09:14.354
who appreciate the finer things.

00:09:14.438 --> 00:09:17.107
Poetry, philosophy, hats.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:19.568
So long, coffin-stuffers!

00:09:27.618 --> 00:09:30.454
Uh... Could one of you coffin-stuffers
please carry me?

00:09:40.505 --> 00:09:41.924
Now, which group of heads

00:09:42.007 --> 00:09:44.509
is good enough for me
to hang out with?

00:09:44.593 --> 00:09:45.928
What do you think, Fry?

00:09:46.011 --> 00:09:47.012
Fry?

00:09:47.095 --> 00:09:48.138
Hmm.

00:09:48.222 --> 00:09:49.306
Hi.

00:09:49.431 --> 00:09:50.515
I'm Claudia Schiffer's head.

00:09:50.599 --> 00:09:51.725
I recognize you.

00:09:51.808 --> 00:09:53.936
Didn't you use to have
a body of some sort?

00:09:54.019 --> 00:09:56.104
Yeah, but it was
holding me back.

00:09:56.188 --> 00:09:57.898
You know, I just
did the cover

00:09:57.981 --> 00:10:00.400
of the Sports Illustrated
swim cap issue.

00:10:00.567 --> 00:10:01.652
Rawrr!

00:10:01.735 --> 00:10:03.237
Well, you're looking great.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:06.281
Thanks. I wouldn't
mind losing a few pounds, though.

00:10:06.365 --> 00:10:07.491
Couldn't hurt.

00:10:10.035 --> 00:10:11.161
Ah!

00:10:11.245 --> 00:10:12.913
US presidents!

00:10:12.996 --> 00:10:15.791
Sturdy shelves,
good security...

00:10:16.959 --> 00:10:18.752
This place has class.

00:10:18.835 --> 00:10:20.045
Hey, sugar cookie!

00:10:20.128 --> 00:10:21.213
You know, legally,

00:10:21.296 --> 00:10:23.757
nothing I can do
counts as sex anymore.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.759
I apologize
for his rudeness, ma'am.

00:10:25.842 --> 00:10:28.303
He gets this way
around meaty-looking women.

00:10:28.739 --> 00:10:29.971
Hey, I remember you.

00:10:30.088 --> 00:10:31.640
I was going to vote
for you one time.

00:10:31.723 --> 00:10:32.975
But voting isn't cool

00:10:33.058 --> 00:10:35.561
so I stayed home alone
and got trashed on Listerine.

00:10:35.644 --> 00:10:37.187
Frankly, I've never felt voting

00:10:37.271 --> 00:10:39.314
to be all that essential
to the process.

00:10:39.398 --> 00:10:41.817
No kidding, Ford.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.694
So then the hooker-bot says,

00:10:43.777 --> 00:10:45.862
"That's not my expansion slot."

00:10:45.946 --> 00:10:47.197
And my friend says,

00:10:47.281 --> 00:10:50.117
"That's not my gold-plated
25-pin connector."

00:10:52.995 --> 00:10:53.996
Oh, Bender.

00:10:54.079 --> 00:10:56.915
Thou robots really cracketh me up.

00:10:56.999 --> 00:10:58.667
You know, I like it here.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:00.794
What's the rent
on one of these jars?

00:11:00.877 --> 00:11:02.921
Sorry, Bender,
but we can't allow

00:11:03.005 --> 00:11:05.033
every Tom, Dick and Harry to move in.

00:11:05.058 --> 00:11:07.578
No offense Jefferson, Nixon and Truman.

00:11:07.603 --> 00:11:09.469
Maybe Mr. Bender can get a spot

00:11:09.553 --> 00:11:11.513
in the closet of presidential losers.

00:11:11.597 --> 00:11:13.432
Bob Dole needs company.

00:11:13.515 --> 00:11:15.893
Larouche won't stop
with the knock-knock jokes.

00:11:15.976 --> 00:11:16.977
Pass.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:18.061
So telleth, Bender,

00:11:18.145 --> 00:11:19.813
what hath happened
to your body?

00:11:19.897 --> 00:11:20.939
I hocked it.

00:11:21.023 --> 00:11:22.691
Hocked it?
Why wouldst thou do that?

00:11:22.774 --> 00:11:24.568
Same reason
you hocked your teeth.

00:11:24.651 --> 00:11:26.987
Ah. Booze money.

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.697
I remember my body.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:32.743
Flabby, pasty-skinned,
riddled with phlebitis.

00:11:32.826 --> 00:11:34.369
A good Republican body.

00:11:34.453 --> 00:11:36.079
God, I loved it.

00:11:36.163 --> 00:11:37.372
I hear that.

00:11:37.456 --> 00:11:39.583
I spent most of my teen years
loving my body.

00:11:40.056 --> 00:11:41.808
Course, it was tough love...

00:11:42.107 --> 00:11:45.005
Fry, he opened up relations with China.

00:11:45.088 --> 00:11:47.049
He doesn't want to hear
about your ding-dong.

00:11:47.132 --> 00:11:49.384
So, Nixon,
even if you miss your body,

00:11:49.468 --> 00:11:51.470
being a head's great, too, right?

00:11:51.553 --> 00:11:52.554
No, son.

00:11:52.638 --> 00:11:54.890
It's a sad and lonely life.

00:11:54.973 --> 00:11:56.934
Great. Now you tell me.

00:11:57.017 --> 00:11:58.393
That's my style.

00:11:58.477 --> 00:12:00.646
I like to kick 'em
when they're down.

00:12:08.779 --> 00:12:11.823
One, zero...

00:12:11.907 --> 00:12:14.952
One, one, zero,
zero, one...

00:12:16.203 --> 00:12:17.663
Bender, what is it?

00:12:17.746 --> 00:12:19.581
What an awful dream.

00:12:19.665 --> 00:12:21.667
Ones and zeros everywhere.

00:12:22.876 --> 00:12:24.920
And I thought I saw a two.

00:12:25.003 --> 00:12:26.463
It was just a dream, Bender.

00:12:26.546 --> 00:12:28.090
There's no such thing as two.

00:12:28.173 --> 00:12:30.008
I know what this is about.

00:12:30.092 --> 00:12:33.345
My body loved me
and I turned its back on it.

00:12:33.428 --> 00:12:37.391
Well, old friend, tie a yellow ribbon
'round your neck

00:12:37.474 --> 00:12:39.393
'cause I'm a-comin' home.

00:12:40.602 --> 00:12:43.063
You sold my body? To who?

00:12:43.146 --> 00:12:44.648
I can't reveal that information

00:12:44.731 --> 00:12:46.066
but you look like a nice robot.

00:12:46.149 --> 00:12:48.610
Tell you what. I'll give you
50 bucks for the kid.

00:12:48.694 --> 00:12:51.113
Hey, my clothes
are worth 50 bucks.

00:12:51.196 --> 00:12:52.197
Deal.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.540
Oh!

00:12:54.992 --> 00:12:56.994
How could I let this happen?

00:12:57.077 --> 00:13:00.372
I can't go through
the rest of my life like this.

00:13:00.455 --> 00:13:02.666
Don't you have
a self-destruct button?

00:13:02.749 --> 00:13:06.336
Yeah... But it's on my body.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.922
What am I going to do?

00:13:11.466 --> 00:13:15.178
I can't stand to see a robot cry.

00:13:15.262 --> 00:13:16.638
Let's watch TV.

00:13:16.722 --> 00:13:18.932
And so, ladies and gentlemen,

00:13:19.016 --> 00:13:21.810
I'm throwing my head
into the ring.

00:13:21.894 --> 00:13:26.398
I'm announcing my candidacy
for the presidency of earth.

00:13:27.691 --> 00:13:28.775
Scoop Chang, Beijing Bugle.

00:13:28.859 --> 00:13:30.611
Sir, the constitution clearly states

00:13:30.694 --> 00:13:33.488
that nobody can be elected
president more than twice.

00:13:33.572 --> 00:13:36.074
That's right... No body.

00:13:36.158 --> 00:13:39.995
But as you can plainly see,
I've got a shiny new body.

00:13:44.124 --> 00:13:46.168
Bender, he's got your body!

00:13:46.251 --> 00:13:49.004
That dirty,
double-crossing bastard!

00:13:49.087 --> 00:13:51.632
How dare he run off
with Richard Nixon.

00:13:54.593 --> 00:13:57.429
Nixon must have bought your body
from the pawnshop.

00:13:57.512 --> 00:13:59.139
Yeah, and that electric guitar.

00:13:59.223 --> 00:14:04.645
Remember what the dormouse said

00:14:06.355 --> 00:14:08.732
feed your head...

00:14:08.815 --> 00:14:12.569
I'm meeting you halfway,
you stupid hippies.

00:14:15.239 --> 00:14:17.241
I am not a crook's head.

00:14:17.324 --> 00:14:19.701
Yeah, you are.
You stole my body!

00:14:19.785 --> 00:14:22.579
Fry, Leela, you got to help me.

00:14:22.663 --> 00:14:24.790
Ordinarily, I'd say no and lecture you

00:14:24.873 --> 00:14:27.834
on how this is your own fault
for being such an idiot.

00:14:27.918 --> 00:14:30.170
But when a robotic Nixon is on the loose,

00:14:30.254 --> 00:14:32.089
we have a duty to take action.

00:14:32.172 --> 00:14:33.548
Idiot.

00:14:46.688 --> 00:14:49.566
Morbo will now introduce
tonight's candidates.

00:14:50.082 --> 00:14:51.958
Puny human number one,

00:14:52.042 --> 00:14:54.336
puny human number two,

00:14:54.711 --> 00:14:57.569
and Morbo's good friend,
Richard Nixon.

00:14:57.594 --> 00:14:59.930
Hello, Morbo.
How's the family?

00:15:00.175 --> 00:15:02.302
Belligerent and numerous.

00:15:02.386 --> 00:15:03.512
Good man.

00:15:03.595 --> 00:15:06.014
Nixon's pro-war and pro-family.

00:15:10.043 --> 00:15:14.047
Great. First he steals my body,
now he's touching my stuff.

00:15:14.131 --> 00:15:17.009
Come on. We've got
to find some way to talk to him.

00:15:19.011 --> 00:15:21.930
Morbo demands an answer
to the following question:

00:15:22.014 --> 00:15:26.101
"If you saw delicious candy
in the hands of a small child

00:15:26.184 --> 00:15:28.937
"would you seize and consume it?"

00:15:29.021 --> 00:15:30.063
Unthinkable!

00:15:30.147 --> 00:15:31.899
I wouldn't think of it!

00:15:31.982 --> 00:15:33.442
What about you, Mr. Nixon?

00:15:33.525 --> 00:15:36.528
I remind you,
you are under a truth-o-scope.

00:15:37.613 --> 00:15:38.864
Well...

00:15:38.947 --> 00:15:41.533
The question is vague.

00:15:41.617 --> 00:15:45.120
You don't say what kind of candy,

00:15:45.245 --> 00:15:47.539
whether anyone is watching...

00:15:49.291 --> 00:15:52.461
At any rate,
I certainly wouldn't harm the child.

00:15:57.841 --> 00:15:59.968
You scored big points tonight, sir.

00:16:00.093 --> 00:16:03.680
What are you talking about?
They ate me alive out there.

00:16:03.764 --> 00:16:05.807
Yes, but your body
stayed on message

00:16:05.891 --> 00:16:08.810
and that message is,
"Look at my shiny new body."

00:16:08.894 --> 00:16:10.145
The robots ate it up.

00:16:10.229 --> 00:16:12.731
You've got real charisma
from the neck down.

00:16:12.814 --> 00:16:14.483
Nixon with charisma.

00:16:14.566 --> 00:16:16.151
My God!

00:16:16.235 --> 00:16:18.153
I can rule the universe!

00:16:19.696 --> 00:16:22.491
Give me my body back,
you two-bit thief!

00:16:22.574 --> 00:16:24.826
Now, look here,
you drugged-out communist,

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:27.704
I paid for this body
and I'd no sooner return it

00:16:27.788 --> 00:16:30.916
than I would my little
cocker spaniel dog, Checkers.

00:16:31.375 --> 00:16:33.001
Shut up, damn it!

00:16:33.085 --> 00:16:34.294
Please, Mr. Nixon.

00:16:34.378 --> 00:16:36.713
We're appealing to
your sense of decency.

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:39.841
Very good!

00:16:42.636 --> 00:16:45.264
Seriously, though,
I'm never giving back this body.

00:16:45.347 --> 00:16:48.725
Now, beat it, before I get
Cambodian on your asses!

00:16:52.104 --> 00:16:54.147
It's hopeless.

00:16:54.231 --> 00:16:57.943
We might as well turn in my head
for the 5 cent deposit.

00:16:58.026 --> 00:16:59.152
No way.

00:16:59.236 --> 00:17:02.030
I'm not letting my best friend
get recycled.

00:17:02.114 --> 00:17:04.366
Not for 5 cents,
not for 500 cents.

00:17:04.449 --> 00:17:05.867
Leela, I've got a plan.

00:17:05.951 --> 00:17:07.286
I've got a better plan.

00:17:15.586 --> 00:17:17.754
Why would Nixon stay
at the Watergate?

00:17:17.838 --> 00:17:20.299
They give you a discount
if you've been here before.

00:17:33.687 --> 00:17:36.106
Keep going.
We're right behind you.

00:17:37.316 --> 00:17:40.110
Whoa, mama. Get a room, you two.

00:17:40.193 --> 00:17:41.403
We're in a room!

00:17:41.486 --> 00:17:43.780
Well, then, lose some weight.

00:17:50.829 --> 00:17:56.001
Oh, yeah, you women's libbers
really know how to party.

00:17:56.084 --> 00:17:57.461
There I am.

00:18:02.299 --> 00:18:04.051
Hey, Betty Friedan,

00:18:04.134 --> 00:18:07.721
send a little of
that lotion my way.

00:18:07.804 --> 00:18:10.057
Okay, almost got it.

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:11.350
Steady...

00:18:11.433 --> 00:18:12.643
Steady...

00:18:12.726 --> 00:18:14.436
Don't panic.

00:18:16.021 --> 00:18:17.022
Ooh.

00:18:17.147 --> 00:18:18.523
Uh-oh.

00:18:22.653 --> 00:18:24.154
What the...

00:18:27.324 --> 00:18:30.452
You shaggy peaceniks
have some nerve.

00:18:30.535 --> 00:18:32.037
I'm just here
for what's mine.

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.622
Don't make me kick your neck.

00:18:33.705 --> 00:18:35.249
Bring it on, soup can.

00:18:40.837 --> 00:18:42.631
All right, break it up, you two.

00:18:44.466 --> 00:18:45.467
That's it!

00:18:45.551 --> 00:18:46.885
You're all going to jail

00:18:46.969 --> 00:18:49.346
and don't expect me
to grant a pardon

00:18:49.429 --> 00:18:50.806
like that sissy Ford.

00:18:50.889 --> 00:18:52.391
You'll never pardon anybody

00:18:52.474 --> 00:18:54.977
because you'll never
get elected president.

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:58.730
The voters of earth aren't the pea-brained
idiots they were back in your time.

00:18:58.814 --> 00:19:00.983
Oh, no? Well, listen here, missy.

00:19:01.066 --> 00:19:04.403
Computers may be twice as fast
as they were in 1973,

00:19:04.486 --> 00:19:08.240
but your average voter is
as drunk and stupid as ever.

00:19:08.323 --> 00:19:10.284
The only one who's changed is me.

00:19:10.367 --> 00:19:12.619
I've become bitter and, let's face it,

00:19:12.703 --> 00:19:14.663
crazy over the years.

00:19:14.746 --> 00:19:16.707
And once I'm swept into office,

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:19.835
I'll sell our children's organs
to zoos for meat

00:19:19.918 --> 00:19:24.006
and I'll go into people's houses
at night and wreck up the place.

00:19:26.466 --> 00:19:28.176
Well, he lost my vote.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:30.554
Like one vote
ever made a difference.

00:19:30.637 --> 00:19:32.055
Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:19:32.139 --> 00:19:34.725
I'm going to inch myself
over to the phone

00:19:34.808 --> 00:19:36.059
and call the police.

00:19:38.353 --> 00:19:40.355
Not so fast, Nixon!

00:19:40.439 --> 00:19:42.900
Are you familiar with audio tape?

00:19:44.943 --> 00:19:47.696
Uh-oh. I don't like where this is heading.

00:19:47.779 --> 00:19:49.990
And I'll go into people's houses at night

00:19:50.073 --> 00:19:51.116
and wreck up the place.

00:19:53.911 --> 00:19:56.455
My God, I really sound like that?

00:19:56.538 --> 00:19:59.207
I thought my voice had
more of a Clark Gable quality.

00:20:00.626 --> 00:20:01.710
The jig's up, Nixon.

00:20:01.793 --> 00:20:03.545
We'll trade you the tape
for the body.

00:20:03.629 --> 00:20:05.797
Oh, expletive deleted.

00:20:05.881 --> 00:20:07.549
You've got a deal.

00:20:07.633 --> 00:20:10.219
Hey, I've got one last thought.

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:20.270
Ah! It's good to be back
in one piece again...

00:20:20.354 --> 00:20:23.565
Except I can't get these
damn bumper stickers off.

00:20:23.649 --> 00:20:25.567
The sheer drama
of this election

00:20:25.651 --> 00:20:27.110
has driven voter turnout

00:20:27.194 --> 00:20:30.197
to its highest level in centuries. 6%.

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:33.784
Exit polls show evil underdog
Richard Nixon trailing

00:20:33.867 --> 00:20:35.786
with an estimated zero votes.

00:20:35.869 --> 00:20:38.080
Yes! The system works.

00:20:38.163 --> 00:20:39.248
The time is 7:59

00:20:39.331 --> 00:20:41.833
and the robot polls
are now opening...

00:20:41.917 --> 00:20:43.502
And the robot vote is in.

00:20:43.585 --> 00:20:44.920
Nixon has won!

00:20:45.003 --> 00:20:46.505
- Get out of town!
- No!

00:20:46.588 --> 00:20:48.090
Why would robots vote for Nixon

00:20:48.173 --> 00:20:50.300
now that he's just a head in a jar?

00:20:51.843 --> 00:20:55.931
I give you the next president
of earth!

00:20:59.768 --> 00:21:01.853
Nixon's back!

00:21:04.064 --> 00:21:07.943
I can't believe it.
He won by a single vote.

00:21:08.026 --> 00:21:09.403
Well, it ain't my fault.

00:21:09.486 --> 00:21:11.530
I'm a non-voting felon,
thank you.

00:21:11.613 --> 00:21:14.116
Well, it's not my fault, either,
'cause I forgot to vote.

00:21:14.199 --> 00:21:18.036
Oh, Crud, I knew there was
something I meant to do today.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:22.457
Morbo congratulates
our gargantuan cyborg president.

00:21:22.541 --> 00:21:25.669
May death come quickly
to his enemies.

00:21:34.177 --> 00:21:37.556
Who's kicking who around now?

00:21:46.648 --> 00:21:47.774
Knock, knock.